.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-REGISTER 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-register \- create a new Euclid user account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam register
.BR \-\-user | \-u
.I USERID
.BR \-\-email | \-e
.I EMAIL
.BR \-\-password | \-p
.I PASSWORD
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new user account via the eam service's
.I register
action.
.PP
The caller must be authenticated as an administrator (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)),
.B except
when the server's user store is completely empty: the very first account
ever registered is allowed through unauthenticated and is automatically
promoted to administrator, so there is always a way to bootstrap the first
account on a fresh server.
.PP
The created user's JSON representation is printed to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSERID\fR
User ID for the new account. Required.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-email " " \fIEMAIL\fR
Email address for the new account. Required.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-password " " \fIPASSWORD\fR
Password for the new account. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The account was created.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller is
not an authenticated administrator, the user ID is already taken, or the
server otherwise rejected the request. If the failure was an expired or
invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored credentials file is removed;
run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
Bootstrap the first account on an empty server (no login required):
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam register \e
    --user admin --email admin@example.com --password 'change-me'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Register a second account once logged in as an administrator:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam login \e
    --user admin --password 'change-me'

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam register \e
    --user jdoe --email jdoe@example.com --password 'hunter2'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-users (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-user (1)
